# Local single-origin reverse proxy for verification (Milestone 5). Plain http on a loopback port: this proves routing,
# cookies and WebSocket upgrades behind ONE origin; it does NOT prove TLS (terminate TLS in front of this in a real
# deployment, or give Caddy a real hostname and let it manage certificates).
#
#   /api/*  /socket.io/*  /health/*  -> NestJS API (api:3001)
#   everything else                  -> Next.js web app (web:3000)
#
# Caddy's reverse_proxy overwrites client-supplied X-Forwarded-* headers unless the peer is a trusted proxy, so the API
# (TRUST_PROXY_HOPS=1) sees exactly one value: the address that connected to this proxy. WebSocket upgrades (Socket.IO
# is WebSocket-only here) are passed through automatically, with Origin and Cookie intact. No access log is enabled on
# purpose: request lines can contain filter values.
# /health/* is routed only so the smoke test can reach it through the proxy; expose it to your orchestrator, not to users.
{
	admin off
	auto_https off
}

:8080 {
	@api path /api/* /socket.io /socket.io/* /health/*
	handle @api {
		reverse_proxy api:3001
	}
	handle {
		reverse_proxy web:3000
	}
}
